    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0201" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14283: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-03T16:00:00+00:00">November 3, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 3—1:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1280. (1) The information embodied in your 672, November 2, 3 p.m., was brought
                    to Cadogan’s<anchor n="60" xml:id="d239-f1"/> attention this afternoon.</p>
                <p>(2) He expressed pleasure over this evidence of our interest in the question and
                    stated that it was almost certain that the British Government would desire to
                    instruct Craigie to make similar but separate representations. He thought that
                    he could let us know the Foreign Office’s decision by tomorrow.</p>
                <pb facs="0202" n="198" xml:id="pg198"/>
                <p>(3) He expressed the hope that Grew would meanwhile hold his hand.</p>
                <p>Copy by mail to Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d239-f1" n="60" xml:id="d239-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Alexander M. J. Cadogan, British Permanent Under Secretary of State for
                    Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
